11.0.0 — every value exact in s, Hz and note value, a tempo calculator, the note grid back over the Field, a simpler Instrument page and Song menu

New since 10088, built by the Echoel Studio run; nothing here is device-verified yet.
- Every value field reads exactly: times in s, rates and pitches in Hz, and the note value at the
  song's tempo. Nothing is rounded for you. A long value is shown compact and ends in "…"; a long
  press shows the full value, with Copy. Moving a control lands on a readable grid; the number
  pad takes milliseconds for a time and hundredths of a hertz up to 1 kHz.
- "Tempo Calculator…" in the Song menu: the song's tempo or one you type or tap, every note value
  in s, ms and Hz (straight, dotted, triplet), bar length, samples and frames, the tempo from a
  length, pitch and wavelength. "Use for Song" sets the tempo.
- The note grid is back over the full-screen Field: "Note Grid" in its bar. The song's scale
  across, an octave a row, the lowest at the bottom. A touch plays the track the keys play, so
  any instrument or plugin on it sounds, a take records it and MPE Out sends it. "Hold" keeps
  notes, the octave buttons move the grid. Every sounding note lights its cell as a cloud in the
  picture. The drops under a finger are held back in this build: their red light is not yet
  bounded under three flashes a second.
- The Instrument page leads with the Field and the sound. While no body source is on, the Body
  Voice is off and the tempo is Fixed, the body is one row, "Body: Off", that opens to its
  controls. The safety sentence stands where a body source is chosen.
- A shorter Song menu with one word per function, and Learn reachable from the first screen. A
  plain store page. Arrange keeps its place. The on-screen keys name the track they play and
  offer the others.
- No two tracks share a name by accident; where two do, the track list offers "Number Them".
- "Report…" in the Song menu shows the app's own report of this session and shares it only when
  you do; "Run Self-Test" on that page measures this device, offline.
- An edit the song refuses in the Mixer or the Session says why. Escape closes the Region, Color
  and Subtitles sheets. Voice Control answers to the letters on Mute, Solo and MIDI Learn.
- Tone systems: a key just under the root now sounds the tonic above in sléndro, pélog, Hirajōshi
  and Archytas, and the tables come from their exact definitions. A song in one of these systems
  sounds different on that key than in 10088.
- The camera pulse moves the song as measured; it is no longer rounded to a whole beat first.
  The number shown stays whole.
- Songs are now written as format 5 (it can hold recorded body movement; this build does not
  record it yet). A song saved by this build does not open in 10088 or earlier. Songs from
  earlier builds open unchanged.

Previous: 10088. A green commit that changes this file uploads build 10000 + run number. A test
list, not a source for claims (ContentPipeline/CLAIMS.md).

Five checks, each one action and a yes or no. A screen recording of all five is the best answer.
1. Field, full screen, "Note Grid" on: play with several fingers, slide, switch "Hold" on and
   off, leave the full screen. Does every note end, do the clouds follow the notes, and does the
   bar fit on a phone held upright?
2. Open a delay or any effect with a time: is the value shown in s with its note value, and does
   a long press show the full value with Copy?
3. Song menu, "Tempo Calculator…": type the tempo of a song you know. Do the note values match
   the calculator you trust, digit for digit?
4. Instrument page with the body off: are Sound and Mood in sight without scrolling, does one tap
   on "Body: Off" open it, and is the safety sentence above the body sources shown whole?
5. Sixteen bars in two to five minutes, as before: a beat, a bass line or a chord, then Play.
   Where does it stop being possible or pleasant?

The open checks of 10079 to 10088 rest until this recording exists.
